Things were pretty easy for Bymekyr in the beginning, but she had some
obstacles to overcome.  First of all, since she was a packrat, the 
lack of a bag of holding until Sokoban was annoying, and she ended up 
leaving stuff in chests and large boxes.  Also, there were no altars 
in the early levels.

Wanting to get a better weapon, Bymekyr decided to attempt to obtain 
Excaliber.  For some reason, she thought that at level 4 she could get
it, so she used up every fountain in the main branch.  All she got 
from this was a jagged, rusty hunk of metal.  Oh well... she could 
still tear apart most monsters anyway.

Once she got to the first fork in the dungeon, she attempted the 
mines.  It appeared that most adventurers met their doom there because
many piles o' bones were to be found.  The only really useful thing 
found there was a wand of polymorph.  Interceptor the large dog soon 
became Gargamel the Gargoyle.  Gargy was a close companion for about 
half of the adventure.

Eventually, a bones level with lots of nasties was reached, so Bymekyr
turned back and tackled Sokoban.  She had to crush a boulder once, but
otherwise had no issues.  The bag of holding found there was the only
bag found in the entire game.

Now that she had carrying capacity and extra levels, Bymekyr cruised 
to Mine Town.  Once Gargy eliminated the guard, a watery tart hiding 
in the fountain gave my Valkyrie Excaliber!  Once she finished the 
mines and got the luckstone, everything was a piece of cake.  With all
the obtained gold from dead shopkeepers and bones piles, divine 
protection was bought for a naked AC of 1. 

After the Oracle's level, an altar was finally found, and plenty of 
!oHW was created as well as everyone's favorite warhammer.  Bymekyr 
was now unstoppable.  The quest was cake, as was Medusa.

With her magic flute, Bymekyr entered the castle, slaying all 
inhabitants.  With the wand of wishing, six things were obtained: +3 
GDSM, [GoP, [BoS, MM, +3 [HS, and a blessed figurine of an Archon 
(Gargy stepped onto a level teleporter, never to be found again). 
Unfortunately, Arnie the Archon polymorphed into Arnie the Violet
Fungus, so she zapped him into a female arch lich (which is not that 
swell of a pet compared to an Archon).

Though things were peachy between Bymekyr and her god, she made a 
terrible mistake with the best of intentions.  Arnie killed the priest
of Moloch in the VotD, so Bymekyr decided to convert the altar.  After
all, she wasn't in Gehennom yet.  Boy, that pissed Tyr off.  He would 
remain so 'til the race for space.

Bymekyr didn't really find Hell boring until after finding the VS.  
She then realized that she had no idea where the Wizard's tower was.  
It took quite some time to find it.  No ?oG were ever found, so the 
annoying Liches constantly plagued her until she found it.  Rodney 
went down after a short fight, and Bymekyr now had the necessary 
implements to get the Amulet.  She almost bit the dust getting it but 
finally killed the high priest and held the Amulet victoriously 
overhead.

But after this moment of victory, she threw caution to the wind.

First, she tried to enchant some armor with a ?oEA.  Not realizing 
that her boots were cursed and weren't removed, she accidentally 
vaporized them.  CRAP!  Immediately afterward, she placed a 
/oCancellation in the (BoH.  Her entire ascension kit was ruined, and 
she didn't follow the wisdom of keeping a stash.

Sighing, she decided to at least give Moloch as much grief as 
possible before she bit the dust.  Luckily, another pair of boots was 
found the next level up.  However, she was still having problems 
keeping unburdened.  She decided the best thing to do to prevent 
cursing was to carry a large box with her.

Once she got back to the castle, she realized that her =oIA and =oS 
were cursed, and there was no way to cross the trap doors since she 
couldn't don the =oL.  She traversed back down in Hell looking for a 
solution until she finally figured out that she could just zap 
herself with a /oLightning.

The trip upward was tedious, and she felt as thought she was 
trudging through the same levels again and again.  /oT and !oFH were 
found along the way, but not many could be carried without burdening.

The Wizard and arch liches were difficult trials for her, and a few 
times she had to chug down a potion of full healing.  She worried 
that she would be destroyed in the Astral plane.

The Orb of Fate told Bymekyr where the portal on the Plane of Earth 
was, but it didn't work once on Fire and ran out of charges.  So she 
played hide and seek with the Amulet instead.  The monsters on Fire 
were so ineffective that she only killed them if they were standing 
in the way.

Air took quite some time, and the air elementals were pretty nasty.

Water was really annoying with no c?oGD or crystal ball.  Bymekyr 
must have killed the Wizard five times on that plane.  She was amazed 
at how beautiful and alien a place it was, though.  

Finally, the final portal was found and she found herself standing on 
Astral.  Death died once clonked on the head enough times, and Famine 
and Pestilence were zapped by a /oDeath.  Famine was Bymekyr's 
biggest worry since she didn't have much food.

Rather than walk up to each altar, Bymekyr looked for a friendly 
priest in each direction.  Once she found one from Tyr, she waded to 
the altar and offered up the Amulet.

